. Update package information
sudo dnf update -y
2. Install HTTPD
sudo dnf install httpd -y
3. Start HTTPD
sudo systemctl start httpd
4. Enable it at boot
sudo systemctl enable httpd
5. Check the service
sudo systemctl status httpd

You should see:

Active: active (running)
6. Test locally
curl http://localhost

You should get the Apache test page HTML.

7. Create your own test page
echo "Welcome to CloudForge Training Institute" | sudo tee /var/www/html/index.html

Then:

curl http://localhost

Expected:

Welcome to CloudForge Training Institute
8. If this is an AWS EC2 RHEL server

Allow HTTP traffic through the Security Group:

Type: HTTP
Protocol: TCP
Port: 80
Source: 0.0.0.0/0

If firewalld is running on the RHEL server:

sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=http
sudo firewall-cmd --reload

Then access:

http://<EC2-Public-IP>
Quick installation

If you just want the commands for your CloudWatch log-testing lab:

sudo dnf install httpd -y
sudo systemctl enable --now httpd
echo "CloudForge Test Server" | sudo tee /var/www/html/index.html
sudo systemctl status httpd
